KNOWNBUG libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp17 --stdlib libc++
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ run time: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
could not be evaluated
static assertion failed
^warning: ignoring
--
With libc++ (18 and Xcode 26) the constant evaluator could not evaluate
`std::string_view{"32"} == "32"': operator== passes the views by value,
copying each with string_view's defaulted copy constructor, which had no
definition yet (only odr-used ones are) and whose argument, the address
of a constexpr object, was not taken as a constant.
